Error [E0918]: `triple` cannot be inlined: its address is taken
  --> tests/ui/inline_always_address_taken.jet:4:1
    |
  4 | #InlineAlways fn triple(x: Int) -> Int {
    | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `#InlineAlways` promises every call to `triple` expands in place — but `triple` is also used as a plain value somewhere (stored, returned, or passed as a callback), and a value needs a real function to point at.
 Fix: drop `#InlineAlways`, or call `triple` directly instead of through a value.
